<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20982] mkfs.lustre overwrites non-Lustre filesystems and signatures without --reformat</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20982</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On ldiskfs, &lt;tt&gt;mkfs.lustre&lt;/tt&gt; formats a device that already holds a non-Lustre signature (xfs, ext4, LVM2_member, linux_raid_member, crypto_LUKS, swap or a partition table) without &lt;tt&gt;-&lt;del&gt;reformat&lt;/tt&gt; and without a warning. The data on the device is lost. Other common formatters refuse in this case unless forced: &lt;tt&gt;mkfs.xfs&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;-f&lt;/tt&gt;), &lt;tt&gt;mdadm --create&lt;/tt&gt; (prompts, &lt;tt&gt;&lt;/del&gt;-run&lt;/tt&gt;), &lt;tt&gt;pvcreate&lt;/tt&gt; (&lt;tt&gt;-f&lt;/tt&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
